Okay

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:49.900
Time for eating! I don't know where Mary Jane is

00:20:49.900 --> 00:20:51.720
she's been out a while...

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:56.660
Oh! Mary Jane is back and Mary Jane looks in terrible shape

00:20:56.660 --> 00:20:59.060
but she found a lot of food!

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:04.040
And that is what I like- FOUR cans of food!

00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:06.480
Might as well pack for another expedition

00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:09.180
Timmy got back to the shelter from his expedtion and looked fine

00:21:09.180 --> 00:21:12.680
but it turned out he had hurt his hand on a piece of rusty metal and the wound was INFECTED

00:21:12.680 --> 00:21:14.500
doesn't look like it's healing up- we have to PATCH IT?

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:16.180
WITH AN AXE!?

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:19.800
I HAVE TO CUT HIS HAND OFF!? NO TIMMY! NOOO!

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:22.280
Oh.

00:21:23.460 --> 00:21:24.900
Oh, I guess it's fine.

00:21:25.300 --> 00:21:26.560
He looks.. okay.

00:21:26.560 --> 00:21:30.140
Timmy was very brave about the idea of cleaning up his wound with a heated axe blade

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:31.680
It was a bit painful, but it was soon over

00:21:31.940 --> 00:21:34.740
The axe is in no shape to be used again, but Timmy seems much better!

00:21:34.740 --> 00:21:39.740
Oh! I thought we were gonna cut something OFF

00:21:39.740 --> 00:21:41.360
We should go outside, how about little Tim-Tim?

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:43.680
He did okay last time, why not this time?

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:46.140
What could he bring?

00:21:46.520 --> 00:21:50.100
[weird accent] Could he bring ze flashlighte?

00:21:50.100 --> 00:21:53.760
Maybe nozing would be good for him, I cannot really risk anyzing.

00:21:56.740 --> 00:22:00.040
Yeah, I'm gonna give him nothing 'cause I don't want him to loose nothing.

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:05.200
Actually, maybe we shouldn't send anyone out on an expedition, we don't exactly really NEED anything at the moment?

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:05.720
And

00:22:05.720 --> 00:22:08.300
I want to make sure they get food before they go out

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:11.360
Because that might affect their survival chances. I dont know?

00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:13.960
Ughh, Dolor-Ughh, Mary Jane, come on!

00:22:13.960 --> 00:22:16.640
Mary Jane is starving... caught something nasty...

00:22:16.640 --> 00:22:19.360
Goddammit, Mary Jane, why do you do that to yourself?

00:22:21.580 --> 00:22:23.420
Oh shit, everyone looks bad.

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:25.680
I-I guess Mary Jane...

00:22:27.140 --> 00:22:28.180
did miss out...

00:22:28.180 --> 00:22:29.780
But I'm just going to feed everyone today

00:22:30.340 --> 00:22:32.340
And then cycle back on the 29th

00:22:33.980 --> 00:22:36.860
"A young woman dressed in whit knocked on our door today, telling us a story of her missing twin brother,

00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:44.740
- who is most likely held captive."  She knows that we're good and trustworthy people and believes we can rescue her sibling, it might be the beginning of a solid friendship.

00:22:45.040 --> 00:22:47.200
Okay! Timmy, we're gonna trust you with this one.

00:22:47.560 --> 00:22:48.260
Gooou

00:22:51.420 --> 00:22:53.420
Oh, you're back. You're still alive. Good.

00:22:53.540 --> 00:22:54.260
Let's see.

00:22:54.260 --> 00:22:57.780
The woman quickly called a group of friends and we set out for what turned out to be a successful mission.

00:22:57.780 --> 00:23:02.880
Finding the lost twin brother wasn't a problem, he was hanging on top of some antenna trying to escape

00:23:02.880 --> 00:23:07.720
In the duel with the Bandit leader he lost a hand, but the group quickly tended to his injuries... thanked us a hundred times...

00:23:07.720 --> 00:23:08.700
Okay thats good

00:23:09.340 --> 00:23:11.180
Timmy's going outsiiiiide

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:15.760
Timmy's taking nothing 'cause I don't trust Timmmyyyy!

00:23:15.760 --> 00:23:20.300
Group of doctors knocked on our door today requesting some supplies that would be helpful....

00:23:20.420 --> 00:23:21.860
We do have extra water

00:23:22.380 --> 00:23:27.740
They offer a medkit which would be UNBELIEVABLY helpful if they did that! Please

00:23:28.520 --> 00:23:29.020
No?

00:23:29.020 --> 00:23:30.200
They didn't give us anything in return.

00:23:31.200 --> 00:23:32.000
Wonderful.

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:33.120
Great.

00:23:33.920 --> 00:23:35.840
Glad about that that is cool.

00:23:35.840 --> 00:23:38.920
Every new smell attacks our noses, there isn't much else we can miss.

00:23:38.920 --> 00:23:43.900
So when a single block fell from the wall it revealed a tight opening our senses were immediately invaded by....

00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:46.360
We should probably check that hole out and see what the smell is

00:23:46.580 --> 00:23:47.080
Yeah!

00:23:47.680 --> 00:23:50.640
Best not to ignore weird smells in the walls!

00:23:50.640 --> 00:23:53.100
And it was soup that I could spare not water

00:23:53.100 --> 00:23:54.300
We're fuuuuudged

00:23:54.300 --> 00:23:58.320
We approached the hole cautiously 'n what happened next gave us a heart attack some crazed rodent...

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:01.320
pushed our radio...

00:24:02.720 --> 00:24:03.440
I'M ON EASY

00:24:05.160 --> 00:24:06.440
I'M PLAYING ON EASY

00:24:07.640 --> 00:24:09.480
I'M PLAYING ON FRIGGIN EASY

00:24:10.240 --> 00:24:12.080
WHAT MORE DO YOU WANT FROM ME

00:24:13.760 --> 00:24:14.960
Ohh there's timmy

00:24:17.180 --> 00:24:17.980
[deep sigh]

00:24:19.280 --> 00:24:22.220
Mary Jane loves cards...back from the wasteland..

00:24:22.680 --> 00:24:24.520
Got three bottles of water!

00:24:25.760 --> 00:24:26.260
Good!

00:24:26.260 --> 00:24:32.620
We brought some strange looking people back to our doorstep. They claimed to be wizards and were willing to trade useful supplies for a few...

00:24:32.620 --> 00:24:37.280
weird trinkets. After hearing them out, we decided to look around our shelter for the items they wanted

00:24:37.280 --> 00:24:42.960
They were really ecstatic about purchasing an old pair of socks, which had been lying in the corner for some time, livin' their own life

00:24:42.960 --> 00:24:48.900
The wizards got them in exchange for a few bottles of water, one of them placed the socks on her ears, and started to dance

00:24:48.900 --> 00:24:51.700
They really wanted to SELL US A RADIO!!!!!!!

00:24:53.100 --> 00:24:53.740
YEAAAHHH

00:24:54.480 --> 00:24:56.720
I LIKE THIS! THIS IS COOL! ALRIGHT

00:24:58.480 --> 00:24:59.280
This is good

00:24:59.280 --> 00:25:03.140
This is good. This is good. This Is Good. This is good. This is GOOOD

00:25:03.320 --> 00:25:04.120
This is good

00:25:04.120 --> 00:25:09.000
So I fed them on the 33rd so that means the 38th is the next time we send some people out

00:25:09.400 --> 00:25:13.800
Dolores you're going out with nothing again because I don't trust

00:25:13.800 --> 00:25:16.380
The Army broadcast interrupted with our breakfast

00:25:16.380 --> 00:25:18.900
Geographical coordinates... sign we're still alive - okay!

00:25:18.900 --> 00:25:21.340
This is good! We got coordinates 'cause we got a map!

00:25:22.880 --> 00:25:23.520
We got it!

00:25:23.520 --> 00:25:24.700
Wa-wa-wkawoijasdj

00:25:25.080 --> 00:25:25.640
Wegotit

00:25:26.000 --> 00:25:26.500
okay

00:25:26.500 --> 00:25:30.960
A  quick glance at the map gave us all the information we needed We also managed to send a message in a bottle.

00:25:30.960 --> 00:25:32.260
This is good, this is good.

00:25:32.600 --> 00:25:35.380
Why is Timmy sick? God dammit, why does everyone get sick?

00:25:35.380 --> 00:25:39.020
How do they expect us to be able to keep people alive??

00:25:39.020 --> 00:25:42.160
"The wasteland is full of surprises, like this man on the other side of our door,

00:25:42.160 --> 00:25:45.360
knocking and claiming that he is willing to offer a lot for decent ammunition.

00:25:45.360 --> 00:25:45.860
Shall we trade?"

00:25:46.120 --> 00:25:46.620
Sure!

00:25:46.620 --> 00:25:48.620
Why not? What else do we have to lose?

00:25:48.620 --> 00:25:50.700
If he didn't give us a medkit, I will..

00:25:51.100 --> 00:25:52.380
do things I never thought I do..

00:25:52.540 --> 00:25:55.060
OOOOOOKKKKKAAAAAAAAAY.

00:25:56.580 --> 00:25:57.080
WELL.

00:25:57.140 --> 00:25:59.740
That is not as good as I hoped it would be.

00:26:00.720 --> 00:26:02.520
And apparently Mary Jane is gone.

00:26:02.520 --> 00:26:03.540
What happened to Mary Jane?

00:26:03.900 --> 00:26:04.960
Did she run away?

00:26:04.960 --> 00:26:07.660
"Mary Jane's sickness got worse, and when we weren't able to provide her with medicine,

00:26:07.660 --> 00:26:10.180
she decided it's time to cure whatever she had on her own..."

00:26:10.560 --> 00:26:12.920
Okay! That's another mouth that we don't have to feed!

00:26:12.920 --> 00:26:16.020
So long as I make it out alive because the armory is right around the corner..

00:26:16.020 --> 00:26:18.580
"Friendly soul on the radio was talking about a supply pack she's lost.."

00:26:18.580 --> 00:26:21.360
We get 2 water, 1 soup, and 1 amro.

00:26:22.240 --> 00:26:22.820
Yay.

00:26:23.300 --> 00:26:24.140
That is good.

00:26:24.520 --> 00:26:26.420
Boy scout handbook. Yeaaaahh.

00:26:26.420 --> 00:26:28.420
Wait, we can try fixing the gun?

00:26:28.420 --> 00:26:28.920
YAY!

00:26:28.920 --> 00:26:29.980
[gasp]

00:26:29.980 --> 00:26:30.740
Did we fit the--

00:26:30.740 --> 00:26:32.380
OOOOHHHHHH WE DID!

00:26:32.380 --> 00:26:35.380
TIMMY WE DID IT! YOU MIGHT BE GOING OUT OF YOUR GODDAMN MIND

00:26:35.380 --> 00:26:36.760
BUT WE DID IT!

00:26:36.940 --> 00:26:38.080
YEAAAAAHHHHH

00:26:38.240 --> 00:26:39.060
Okay.

00:26:39.060 --> 00:26:42.000
And then the 43rd is when we get to eat and drink.

00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:45.380
Yeah! Hopelly Deloreth cometh back.

00:26:45.380 --> 00:26:47.900
My wife, I think Iove her thtill?

00:26:47.900 --> 00:26:48.840
Not sure at this point.

00:26:49.200 --> 00:26:50.340
We're a month in a hole.

00:26:50.340 --> 00:26:51.380
That'll do something to ya.

00:26:52.360 --> 00:26:55.960
Oh no! "We don't think Dolores is coming back from the surface, it's been too long."

00:26:55.960 --> 00:26:56.760
Shit!

00:26:57.320 --> 00:26:57.820
Well.

00:26:57.820 --> 00:26:58.900
That's not good.

00:26:58.900 --> 00:27:02.840
"We almost forgot about this one time we shared some water with a group of people dressed in lab coats.

00:27:02.840 --> 00:27:07.500
Out of the blue, they came back today and administered us some very healthy looking shots!

00:27:07.500 --> 00:27:10.180
So they WERE real doctors after all..we think?

00:27:10.180 --> 00:27:10.920
OH!

00:27:10.920 --> 00:27:11.820
They gave us shots!

00:27:12.380 --> 00:27:13.120
Did it cure timmy?!

00:27:15.060 --> 00:27:17.060
Yeah! Timmy's just crazy now!

00:27:17.060 --> 00:27:17.780
He's not..

00:27:18.260 --> 00:27:20.580
He's not..he's not sick!

00:27:20.580 --> 00:27:22.580
Uh, let's just have some celebratory food!

00:27:22.580 --> 00:27:24.860
I mean, it's just you and me, tim-tim, for the rest of life!

00:27:25.340 --> 00:27:25.960
Forever.

00:27:25.960 --> 00:27:26.940
This better pay out,

00:27:26.940 --> 00:27:29.960
because god dammit, I haven't come this far to die!

00:27:30.560 --> 00:27:32.180
I came this far to survive!

00:27:32.180 --> 00:27:36.100
Oh boy! "Lady luck smiled on us!We won a vicious game of war.

00:27:36.100 --> 00:27:38.540
The man wasn't too happy about it, but he delivered on his promise."

00:27:38.900 --> 00:27:39.520
Okay!

00:27:39.520 --> 00:27:41.960
"Before the world turned into an unforgiving, dead wasteland,

00:27:41.960 --> 00:27:43.520
we were friends with almost everybody in our town.

00:27:43.520 --> 00:27:46.720
Including, the old man Jim, who would shamble through our street often and always said hello.

00:27:46.720 --> 00:27:50.000
We wanted to visit him once, he gave us an address that took us...Old man Jim is such a joker!

00:27:50.000 --> 00:27:54.140
It appears that he survived the blast, since he's at our door right now, asking if we want to buy a rock.

00:27:54.460 --> 00:27:55.760
Sure! I'll buy a rock!

00:27:55.980 --> 00:27:59.200
Hopefully this doesn't cost me the life of my only son!

00:27:59.520 --> 00:28:00.460
[laughs]

00:28:00.600 --> 00:28:01.540
Wouldn't that be something.

00:28:01.660 --> 00:28:03.660
"We opened the door and greeted the old man with a smile.

00:28:03.660 --> 00:28:06.100
He was eager to show us his bag filled with a rich choice of rocks

00:28:06.100 --> 00:28:08.060
and convinced us to take one for free 'for old times' sake.'

00:28:08.060 --> 00:28:11.000
We agreed...can't complain, it's a good rock...

00:28:11.000 --> 00:28:13.840
claimed it brings us luck, we'll see about that."

00:28:13.840 --> 00:28:14.340
Okay.

00:28:14.340 --> 00:28:17.460
Alright Timmy, you go out. You may be crazy, but I'm not sending myself.

00:28:17.820 --> 00:28:19.820
If anyone's gonna die, it's gonna be you and not me.

00:28:20.840 --> 00:28:21.940
Oh Timmy, you're back.

00:28:21.940 --> 00:28:24.880
You look slightly tired, but..at least you're still as crazy.

00:28:24.880 --> 00:28:26.840
"Our supplies are scarce and our morale is low.

00:28:26.840 --> 00:28:28.460
You can almost smell the desperation in the shelter.

00:28:28.460 --> 00:28:30.220
We're pretty sure there's a small group of survivors nearby,

00:28:30.220 --> 00:28:31.600
mostly old folks from the retirement home.

00:28:31.900 --> 00:28:33.900
It shouldn't be hard to borrow some of their supplies. They're old and.."

00:28:34.120 --> 00:28:35.040
No, I'm not gonna steal!

00:28:35.040 --> 00:28:36.660
We got enough supplies, we're fiiine.

00:28:36.660 --> 00:28:37.820
We don't need to STEAL.

00:28:37.820 --> 00:28:39.820
Oh Timmy, he was always a wild one.

00:28:39.820 --> 00:28:44.860
A shelter is not the best environment for a boy who's hell bent on running around until he can barely breathe.

00:28:44.860 --> 00:28:48.000
He really misses that. He asked if he can go out to the surface, even for a short while.

00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:51.220
This sounds highly dangerous and irresponsible. Should we agree?

00:28:51.220 --> 00:28:52.140
Yeah!

00:28:52.140 --> 00:28:53.800
Get out, Timmy!

00:28:54.080 --> 00:28:55.240
GET OUT!

00:28:56.040 --> 00:28:57.860
You freaking terror!

00:28:58.400 --> 00:28:59.900
Stay out!

00:29:00.260 --> 00:29:01.900
"Timmy can sneak like a secret-agent man,

00:29:01.900 --> 00:29:05.340
but that might not be enough to avoid the band of Raiders camped near our shelter.

00:29:05.340 --> 00:29:06.880
We can probably assume he isn't coming back.

00:29:07.420 --> 00:29:09.780
When we consented, Timmy almost hit his head on the ceiling."

00:29:09.780 --> 00:29:10.840
Probably cause he's crazy.

00:29:10.840 --> 00:29:14.480
"We figured that if he doesn't encounter any savages, mutated beasts or killer mimes,

00:29:14.480 --> 00:29:16.020
he should be fine and back enough soon."

00:29:16.780 --> 00:29:17.380
Yeah!

00:29:17.380 --> 00:29:19.320
He's got the survival instincts of a crazy person!

00:29:19.320 --> 00:29:21.740
"..heard a knock on the door this morning, we held our breath in fear,

00:29:21.740 --> 00:29:24.860
but we soon heard children's voices coming from outside.

00:29:24.860 --> 00:29:27.020
turned out the voices belonged to a pair of girls scouts."

00:29:27.020 --> 00:29:28.620
They offer a boy scout for a map.

00:29:28.620 --> 00:29:29.660
I've used the map!

00:29:30.200 --> 00:29:34.380
I've used the map. I've used the map in both contexts that I needed the map.

00:29:34.380 --> 00:29:37.580
Which was for the radio of the government, and for the twins.

00:29:37.580 --> 00:29:38.560
I need that book.

00:29:39.080 --> 00:29:40.460
I need that book.

00:29:41.340 --> 00:29:43.340
And Ted is a-okay.

00:29:44.540 --> 00:29:46.100
To stay in here

00:29:46.340 --> 00:29:48.340
for as long as he needs to!

00:29:48.340 --> 00:29:49.820
He's got no family left,

00:29:49.820 --> 00:29:51.700
but he was never a family man..

00:29:51.700 --> 00:29:52.440
oh, he's gone crazy.

00:29:52.580 --> 00:29:54.220
"The other day we heard a quiet knock on our door,

00:29:54.220 --> 00:29:56.540
but when we opened it, it was only a suitcase and no one around,

00:29:56.540 --> 00:29:57.980
signaled look...[mumbles]" Okay, sure.

00:29:57.980 --> 00:29:59.100
It could kill us, but whatever.

00:29:59.100 --> 00:30:00.920
I--I'ma trusting kinda guy.

00:30:01.060 --> 00:30:01.900
Yup, it was sick.

00:30:01.900 --> 00:30:02.680
Yup, bad soup.

00:30:02.680 --> 00:30:05.280
Good good good great great great. Bad soup.

00:30:06.180 --> 00:30:07.140
Uuuhh..

00:30:08.420 --> 00:30:10.400
"We're about to sleep when we heard scratching from the door.

00:30:10.400 --> 00:30:12.780
At first, it sounded like an angry rat..much worse..

00:30:13.280 --> 00:30:15.100
something is on the other side, we need to act!"

00:30:15.100 --> 00:30:16.440
Lock the damn door!

00:30:16.440 --> 00:30:18.440
At least the lock is gonna be useful. Gosh.

00:30:18.800 --> 00:30:23.360
"We didn't think a small padlock would be enough to stop them, but it turned out to be enough to discourage the unknown attackers.

00:30:23.360 --> 00:30:25.560
It seems that they gave this whole break-in a fair shot,

00:30:25.560 --> 00:30:26.940
but ultimately gave up and left.

00:30:26.940 --> 00:30:28.640
Too bad that padlock is in no shape."

00:30:29.260 --> 00:30:31.380
GREEEEEAAAAAAAT.

00:30:31.380 --> 00:30:32.660
TIME TO EAT,

00:30:32.660 --> 00:30:34.840
CRAZY SICK PERSON, YOU.

00:30:35.100 --> 00:30:37.560
"afraid the army wouldn't get back to us, but they eventually did.

00:30:37.560 --> 00:30:42.600
The next transmission was full of evacuation promises, but it ended as a big 'if'.

00:30:42.600 --> 00:30:47.120
The speaker requested that any survivor groups armed with firearms should dispose of them before they get rescued.

00:30:47.120 --> 00:30:49.540
We don't know what this is about, but it sounds like violating our rights.

00:30:49.540 --> 00:30:51.400
On the other hand, are there any laws left.."

00:30:51.900 --> 00:30:52.400
No!

00:30:52.440 --> 00:30:54.300
I'm not giving up my gun!

00:30:54.460 --> 00:30:55.580
You, screw you!

00:30:55.580 --> 00:30:57.380
That didn't go out well for me last time!

00:30:57.380 --> 00:30:59.380
Eat a dick, gov'ment!

00:30:59.380 --> 00:31:00.920
"We decided to ignore these stupid orders.

00:31:00.920 --> 00:31:02.400
Who are they to tell us what to do?

00:31:02.400 --> 00:31:03.360
The US government?

00:31:03.360 --> 00:31:07.660
Well, they probably are, but that doesn't mean they can take our gun. Over our dead bodies!

00:31:08.280 --> 00:31:08.780
Welp.

00:31:08.980 --> 00:31:10.260
Ted's goin' down.

00:31:11.120 --> 00:31:12.100
Ted ain't doin good.

00:31:13.040 --> 00:31:16.380
"bandit camp nearby..not only are they armed, dangerous, cruel and bloodthirsty.."

00:31:16.800 --> 00:31:17.300
Fine!

00:31:18.860 --> 00:31:19.920
Go get 'em!

00:31:20.300 --> 00:31:21.100
Teddy boy!

00:31:22.740 --> 00:31:23.240
Bang!

00:31:23.420 --> 00:31:24.320
Boom bang!

00:31:24.540 --> 00:31:25.200
Bang!

00:31:25.920 --> 00:31:27.100
Boom bang bang!

00:31:27.940 --> 00:31:29.520
"tried out best, but they had numbers.

00:31:29.520 --> 00:31:32.280
We didn't even manage to reach the supplies, the camp was too well-guarded. The.."

00:31:32.840 --> 00:31:33.400
[sigh]

00:31:34.400 --> 00:31:35.380
Yeah, go get 'em.

00:31:35.380 --> 00:31:36.340
Go get 'em, teddy boy.

00:31:36.340 --> 00:31:37.020
Go get 'em.

00:31:37.020 --> 00:31:37.720
You da man!

00:31:38.240 --> 00:31:39.480
You the man, ted man!

00:31:41.100 --> 00:31:42.460
She's still alive, I guess.

00:31:43.200 --> 00:31:46.540
Oh, "We bravely stormed in, but no one was there. We took a soup can."

00:31:46.880 --> 00:31:48.420
Uh-oh, we lost a soup can.

00:31:48.420 --> 00:31:54.200
"Ted has always had a heart of gold. That's why we weren't really shocked to find him feeding OUR supplies to some disgusting, fat cockroach.

00:31:54.200 --> 00:31:57.380
Both Ted and the bug seemed really happy, so we didn't manage to stay mad for long.

00:31:57.380 --> 00:32:02.280
Although when Ted started sharing jokes and life stories with the cockroach, we became a bit suspicious.

00:32:02.560 --> 00:32:04.300
Oh dead corpse of Delores!

00:32:04.300 --> 00:32:06.540
I think your husband is cheating on you with a cockroach!

00:32:06.720 --> 00:32:07.960
[laughs]

00:32:08.360 --> 00:32:11.080
"Another radio broadcast from the military was a huge shock for us.

00:32:11.080 --> 00:32:14.780
Not only did they postpone our rescue, they also ordered all survivors to get rid of their firearms.

00:32:14.780 --> 00:32:16.780
Are they nuts?! How are we supposed to defend ourselves?!

00:32:16.780 --> 00:32:17.380
It'd better be worth it."

00:32:17.660 --> 00:32:18.420
No!

00:32:18.620 --> 00:32:21.700
I'm not giving up my damn gun!

00:32:22.120 --> 00:32:24.300
It didn't work for me last time,

00:32:24.300 --> 00:32:26.460
you're not gonna make me do it now!

00:32:26.460 --> 00:32:30.460
So screw you, and your frickin' face!

00:32:33.320 --> 00:32:34.460
Nup, there we go.

00:32:34.460 --> 00:32:36.840
I guess we died from sickness, finally!

00:32:37.140 --> 00:32:38.620
God dammit!

00:32:38.760 --> 00:32:41.880
We survived for 68 days..

00:32:42.340 --> 00:32:43.280
How

00:32:43.480 --> 00:32:46.900
we were supposed to survive any longer?!

00:32:46.900 --> 00:32:48.300
I tried. I really tried.

00:32:48.420 --> 00:32:50.420
I need to look up

00:32:50.800 --> 00:32:52.800
guides on this, because

00:32:52.800 --> 00:32:55.620
I am trying my frickin' best...

00:32:57.480 --> 00:32:58.900
Was I supposed to give up my gun?

00:32:58.900 --> 00:33:00.820
I don't know, it didn't work out last time!

00:33:00.820 --> 00:33:03.700
It said that the government quarantined us! What a load of ass.

00:33:03.700 --> 00:33:05.700
So this is the end of 60 seconds for now,

00:33:05.700 --> 00:33:08.400
I'll do another episode where I'm gonna BEAT it,

00:33:08.400 --> 00:33:09.960
ON NORMAL,

00:33:10.420 --> 00:33:12.420
cause I'm gonna..I'm good. I'm good at this.

00:33:12.780 --> 00:33:14.420
I'ma show you guys who's good.

00:33:15.340 --> 00:33:15.840
(very softly) This guy!

00:33:16.240 --> 00:33:18.240
So thank you everybody so much for watching!

00:33:18.500 --> 00:33:20.500
And as always, I will see you..

00:33:20.500 --> 00:33:21.580
in the next video!

00:33:22.340 --> 00:33:23.160
Buh-bye!

